    "annotations": "Verse 1:1 of Surah Al-Fatihah - The Opening Chapter (Makkan, 7 verses). This chapter is the foundation of Islamic prayer and faith. Every Muslim recites Al-Fatihah a minimum of 17 times daily in obligatory prayer (Salah). The Honorable Elijah Muhammad taught that understanding these seven verses was essential to grasping Allah's guidance and the spiritual path for Black America. Al-Fatihah summarizes the entire Quran and establishes the believer's relationship with the Creator—worship, reliance, and guidance.",
    "context": ""
  },
