    "translationMaulana": "Alif Lam Mim",
    "translationYusuf": "Alif-Lam-Mim.",
    "transliteration": "Alif Lam Mim",
    "annotations": "Verse 2:1 - Surah Al-Baqarah (The Cow). Juz 1 spans from Surah Al-Fatihah through Surah Al-Baqarah verse 141. Surah Al-Baqarah is the longest chapter of the Quran (286 verses total) and was revealed in Medina. It addresses believers (Al-Muttaqin), hypocrites (Al-Munafiqun), and disbelievers (Al-Kafirun). The Honorable Elijah Muhammad drew extensively from this Surah in teaching the Nation of Islam about divine guidance, community law, spiritual discipline, and the path to salvation for Black people in America.",
    "context": ""
  },
